    ✓ note — pip was broken because site-packages contained only pip-24.3
Your system Python 3.13 had pip broken: `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages` only contained `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` with no actual `pip` package files, so `import pip` raised `ModuleNotFoundError` and `pip3` failed.

I removed the stale metadata and re-bootstrapped pip from the bundled wheel:

```bash
rm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info
python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip
```

Check:

```bash
$ pip3 --version
pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)

$ python3 -c "import pip; print(pip.__version__)"
24.3.1
```

pip is now importable and usable system-wide. You can install packages again, e.g. `pip3 install <package>`.

